# Week 8 Sunday, missed-edge postmortem (1 PM games), Nov 1 2026
_Written about 5:00 PM ET by Blitz. Research only: no bets, no messages, and no gate, sim or rule changes. Every rule change below is marked **PROPOSAL** and has not been applied._

**Data sources.** Box scores, plays and the DraftKings close come from the public ESPN site API summary, saved in playlogs/2026_wk8/*_box.json. Weather is the Open-Meteo hourly model. The candidate pool is every leg in runs/2026-11-01_*/run_manifest.json. Leg results come from /tmp/g/grades.json.
**nflverse pbp:** Week 8 holds only 2026_08_CAR_GB (TNF). The Sunday pbp is **not posted yet**, so snap and route numbers are UNVERIFIED and the box scores are ESPN only.
**What counts as an edge:** 90+ rush yards, 90+ receiving yards or 8+ catches, 280+ pass yards or 3+ pass TD, 2+ TD, or 120+ scrimmage yards. That gives 25 players. All are listed below; nothing was trimmed.

**Ghost6 name check**
- Tuten: ✅ 16-104, 1 rush TD, plus 2-55 and a receiving TD.
- Higgins: ✅ 10-155, 2 TD.
- Minshew: ✅ 17/23, 188 yards, 3 TD in relief of Brissett. Brissett's last snap was a Q3 4:21 sack, and Minshew was in by Q3 1:35. ESPN's play text doesn't give the reason.
- "Rodriguez TD": **corrected.** It was Chris Rodriguez Jr. (JAX RB2): 6-41, 1 TD, plus 1-17 receiving. He is real but not a wide-margin edge, so he is listed only as RB2 evidence.

## Miss categories (25 edges)
| Category | n | Players |
|-|-|-|
| Never in candidate pool | 4 | Gainwell (TB), Braelon Allen (NYJ), Adonai Mitchell (NYJ), Chase Brown (receptions market; only his rush unders were in the pool) |
| Cut by a gate rule | 9 | Tuten (P7 carry share, p .70), Allgeier (P6 clutch, p .77), Pollard (P6 clutch, p .64), Warren (P14 median, p .59; R+R P4 UNVERIFIED), Gibbs (O79.5 passed but dropped by §11; O87.5 cut by P14 median), Higgins (P14 MISSING model/price), Bowers (P4 ISS-05 TE mapping and P14 MISSING), Cousins (P14 edge +2.4 < +3), Burrow (P14 edge −1.0 / shrink, p .69) |
| Modeled but priced low or on the wrong side | 7 | Irving (lean was U70.5; ran for 170, +99.5), Watson (U210.5 → 324, +113.5), Fannin (U34.5 → 154, +119.5), Geno Smith (U225.5 → 290, +64.5), Cam Ward (U192.5 → 304, +111.5), Chase (U79.5 → 141, +61.5), M. Wilson (U56.5 → 111, +54.5) |
| In-game event | 2 | Minshew (replaced Brissett in Q3; not in the pool), Josh Allen 289 (Lamar left Q1 10:04, so BAL played Fagnano and Huntley; the model had him U247.5 and P14 flagged it MODEL-SUSPECT) |
| Variance | 3 | Dotson (2-95 on 5 targets, one long play; we leaned U25.5), Darnell Washington (3-94; we leaned U20.5), Lawrence (10/14, 3 TD; his U237.5 yards would have **hit** at 210, so the edge was TD efficiency) |

The biggest pattern: **11 of the 25 edges are RBs, or QBs/TEs on the trailing team.** We were on the under for 7 of them.

---
## ATL @ TB: TB 16-0 (TB −2.5, 43.5, rain)
- **Edges:** Irving 27-170; Gainwell 25-140 (not in the pool); Dotson 2-95 (variance).
- **Game-script read:** Rain and an ATL QB collapse (4 INT) drove the script. TB ran 56 times and threw 3 passes. With Egbuka OUT, the vacated targets went to the run game, not to Godwin (0 catches). The sims treated TB as a normal pass split and had Irving as an under (P14 primary-star rule). The model never generated a weather RB2.
- **Signal score 3/4:** weather ✅, ATL run D ✅, total under ✅, margin ❌ (expected 2.5, actual 16).

## CLE @ PIT: PIT 27-6 (PIT −3.5, 38.5)
- **Edges:** Warren 17-143 (cut, P14 median); Watson 27/39 for 324 (we leaned under); Fannin 10-154 on 12 targets (we leaned under; P4 TE UNVERIFIED); D. Washington 3-94 (variance).
- **Game-script read:** PIT built a lead and ran. CLE's trailing-pass volume went to Watson and Fannin. Line 98 (avoid blowout volume) pushed us to unders on the trailing team. That was backwards for the QB and TE.
- **Signal score 2/4:** PIT run edge ✅, under ✅ (33), blowout size ❌, trailing pass volume ❌.

## IND @ JAX: JAX 42-7 (JAX −10.5, 45.5)
- **Edges:** Tuten 16-104 with 2 TD (cut by P7, p .70); Lawrence 3 TD (variance; the yards under would have hit).
- **Game-script read:** JAX ran away with it, and the second-half clock-kill went to Tuten, then Rodriguez. P7 (60% carry share in 3 of the last 4) blocked the lead back in exactly the game script that hands him carries.
- **Signal score 3/4:** spread/blowout ✅, IND run D ✅, JAX RB volume ✅, total ❌ (49 was over).

## LV @ NYJ: LV 38-33 (NYJ −1.5, 46.5)
- **Edges:** Braelon Allen 21-147 (backup with Hall out; not in the pool); Adonai Mitchell 7-142 (deep WR3; not in the pool); Bowers 7-92 with 2 TD (cut, P4/P14); Cousins 247 with 3 TD (cut, P14 edge); Geno 290 (we leaned under).
- **Game-script read:** a shootout and upset. The final was 38-33: Sanders' field goal at 4:31 made it 35-33, and Gay's 53-yarder at 0:27 made it 38-33. The NYJ RB carries Hall vacated went to Allen in full, and we had no backup-RB candidate. Mitchell's deep targets had no pool entry.
- **Signal score 2/4:** LV run D (5.17 YPC) ✅, Hall OUT fallout ✅ (we didn't act on it), total ❌ (71), winner ❌.

## MIN @ DET: DET 19-15 (DET −3.5, 45.5)
- **Edges:** Gibbs 23-153. His O79.5 alt passed but was dropped by §11, and O87.5 was cut by P14 median.
- **Game-script read:** a close, low-scoring game. MIN's blitz rate held down Goff and St. Brown, and DET leaned on Gibbs. The model got the direction right but the sim median sat below the line.
- **Signal score 3/4:** spread ✅, blitz D ✅, Gibbs volume ✅, total ❌ in size (34 vs 45.5; direction right).

## BAL @ BUF: BUF 36-10 (BUF −3, 54.5)
- **Edges:** Josh Allen 289 with 2 TD (in-game event; we had the under).
- **Game-script read:** Lamar went out on his first throw (Q1 10:04, 0/1). Fagnano went 10/21 for 91 with 1 INT and Huntley 2/4 for 0. Flowers had 0 catches, and BUF got short fields. No pregame signal could have caught this. What we lack is any backup-QB fallout pass (see Gaps).
- **Signal score 1/4:** spread direction ✅. Total, margin and BAL passing were all ❌.

## TEN @ CIN: CIN 43-36, OT (CIN −13.5, 45.5)
- **Edges:** Burrow 38/48 for 462 with 5 TD (cut, P14 edge/shrink, p .69); Chase 11-141 on 16 targets (we leaned under; P3 soft-WR-D rule cut it, correctly); Higgins 10-155 with 2 TD (cut, P14); Cam Ward 304 (we leaned under); Pollard 21-117 with 2 TD (cut, P6, p .64); Chase Brown 8 catches (not in the pool for that market).
- **Game-script read:** TEN never got blown out. Pollard's rushing kept them level, and the game went to OT 34 points over the total. The 13.5-point spread drove P6 (no trailing overs) and P13 unders on TEN, and both failed. CIN's passing volume beat every sim.
- **Signal score 1/4:** soft TEN WR D ✅ (P3 itself flagged it). Spread, total and blowout were all ❌.

## ARI @ DAL: ARI 33-30, OT (DAL −7, 54.5; retractable roof, open/closed unknown)
- **Edges:** Allgeier 11-147 with 2 TD (O13.5 cut by P6, p .77); Michael Wilson 8-111 on 15 targets (we leaned under; P4 MISSING); Minshew 188 yards and 3 TD in relief (in-game event).
- **Game-script read:** an underdog upset. ARI threw 46 times, and a QB change in Q3 sparked the comeback. The DAL −7 spread drove the P6 cut on Allgeier, the clearest miss of the day: model p .77, line 13.5, actual 147.
- **Signal score 1/4:** total over ✅. Spread, winner and ARI passing were all ❌.

**Signal score overall: 16/32 (50%).** Pregame signals called the run-heavy favorite scripts (TB, PIT, JAX, DET) at 11 of 16. They called the shootout and upset games (LV@NYJ, BAL@BUF, TEN@CIN, ARI@DAL) at 5 of 16. Weather, run D and vacated-role signals were mostly right, and we acted on none of them through candidate generation. Spread and total signals were the least reliable inputs.

