## Candidate-generation gaps in PHASE_SCRIPT and run_gate
1. **RB2 in blowouts or weather (Tuten, Rodriguez, Gainwell).** PHASE_SCRIPT.md line 92 says RB carries = team rushes × **L3 carry share**, adjusted down when the team trails. Nothing adjusts carries **up** for a projected leader's RB2. Line 106 (rule 5) only blocks backup RB overs when the lead back has a full workload, and no step generates them. Gainwell (rain, 140) and Rodriguez (TD) never reached the pool. The P7 gate (60% carry share in 3 of the last 4) cut Tuten at p .70, and he went for 104.
2. **Backup-QB fallout (BAL: Fagnano, Huntley).** No phase re-projects receivers or the opposing offense when the QB is Q, or for live hedging. Line 6 (step 1, "Identify locked roles") locks roles before kickoff. The Flowers, Bateman and Andrews overs plus the Allen under were all priced as if Lamar played.
3. **Backup CBs, and the Puka cut (LAC CBs out).** Line 9 (2A, HARD) requires PFR defender numbers, and "a leg missing this is cut." Waxter has no PFR sample, so P4 went UNVERIFIED. run_gate.py lines 285–289 (`bad = [... if st in BAD]` → fail unless CUT) then forced the cut. The rule treats a backup CB as *missing data* when it is a *soft matchup that should upgrade the leg*. The same mechanism cut Michael Wilson (P4 MISSING) and Fannin and Bowers (ISS-05 TE mapping).
4. **This-week role check (Tucker).** Line 91 projects targets from **L3 target share** with no check on this week's snaps or routes. Tucker O3.5 went 0 for 0 on 1 target. The pbp isn't posted, so his snap count is UNVERIFIED.
5. **Trailing-team volume (Watson, Fannin, Ward, Geno).** Line 98 ("avoid volume legs ... blown out, except receivers in garbage-time roles") plus the P13 under logic pushed QB and TE unders on trailers. Of the trailing-team pass/rec unders that P13 blocked, 5 of 6 lost; when this block fired it was right. The gap is that no step proposes the matching **over**.

---
## PROPOSALS (not applied; backtested on today's 1 PM data only, small samples)
1. **PROPOSAL: backup or weather RB2 candidate.** When the starter is OUT, rain or wind is flagged, or the team is a 3+ point favorite, add the RB2 rush over to the pool. Backtest: Allen 147 and Gainwell 140 both cleared any line. For 3+ point favorites' RB2s (Dowdle 56, Rodriguez 41, Vaki 65, Davis 30, Perine 10, Goodson 14), **4/6 cleared an assumed 29.5**; no real RB2 lines were in the pool. All triggers combined: **6/8**.
2. **PROPOSAL: P6 "no trailing overs" should not cut rush overs with sim p ≥ .60.** Backtest: P6 clutch-cut overs went 5/13 overall. The ones at p ≥ .60 (Allgeier .77, Pollard .64) went **2/2**.
3. **PROPOSAL: P7 carry-share exemption for the lead back of a 7+ point favorite.** Backtest: Tuten was the only case, 1/1 (P7 overall went 2/5). Too thin; track it for 3 weeks.
4. **PROPOSAL: on backup CBs, P4 UNVERIFIED should become "soft-matchup flag" instead of a cut.** When the mapped defender is a backup with fewer than 8 PFR targets *and* the starter is OUT, allow the over at the team's YPT-allowed rate. Backtest today: Puka was pending at 4 PM, and Wilson 111 on the P4 MISSING side. Sample is **1/1, untestable at scale.** Keep the rule otherwise: TE unders cut for P4 UNVERIFIED went 6/18, so those cuts were mostly right.
5. **PROPOSAL: trailing-team QB/TE overs in projected 3.5+ point losses.** Generate the QB pass yards over and the TE receptions over for the underdog. Backtest (underdog starting QBs with a pool line): Watson 324 vs 210.5 ✅, Ward 304 vs 192.5 ✅, Cousins 247 vs 232.5 ✅, Brissett 119 vs 258.5 ❌ (benched), D. Jones 144 vs 192.5 ❌, Lamar 0 vs 237.5 ❌ (injured). That is **3/6, 3/4 excluding the in-game QB exits**. Fannin 154 was the TE case.
6. **PROPOSAL: deep-speed WR3 vs a weak CB, and move-TEs vs leaky TE Ds.** Adonai Mitchell (7-142), Fannin, Darnell Washington. **Untestable:** there were no lines and no route data (pbp not posted).
7. **PROPOSAL: a this-week role check before any target-share leg.** Require this week's inactives and reported snap or route role (Tucker). **Untestable today** (no snaps).
8. **PROPOSAL: a live backup-QB fallout note.** On a QB injury, re-grade the open legs and mark them hedge candidates. Process only; no backtest.

**Top 5 by evidence:** #1 RB2 (6/8), #2 P6 p≥.60 exemption (2/2), #5 trailing QB overs (3/6, or 3/4 excluding QB exits), #4 backup-CB upgrade (1/1), #3 P7 favorite exemption (1/1).

